============================================================================
[R3] REFUTED: one-window union bound for a whole-S witness.
============================================================================
  Window I = first gap of Vmin = (1/(14 Vmin), 13/(14 Vmin)), |I| = 6/(7 Vmin).
  A 'slow' H-runner u<13 Vmin spins u*|I| = 6u/(7Vmin) < 78/7 ~ 11.1 times in I.
  So even slow runners contribute ~11 wide teeth; sum of danger measures > |I|.
  Hence NO closed-form union/measure bound proves a one-window whole-S witness.
  demo S=[25, 90, 99, 143, 172, 192, 195, 242, 266, 280, 294, 310, 348]: |I|=0.03429, union-bound danger meas in I = 0.068  (exceeds |I|).

